    "task": "Say this better, A minimalist photo settings with flowers",
    "chosen": "A photo composition featuring flowers, characterized by simplicity and minimalistic aesthetics.",
    "rejected": "\"Here are some minimalist settings for photographing flowers:\n\n1. Use a simple background, such as a solid-colored wall or plain sheet, to draw attention to the flowers.\n2. Keep the composition simple by including only a few flowers in the frame.\n3. Experiment with different angles and perspectives, such as shooting from above or below.\n4. Use a wide aperture (low f-stop number) to create a shallow depth of field, which will blur the background and make the flowers stand out.\n5. Adjust the white balance to bring out the colors of the flowers.\n6. Use a tripod to keep the camera steady and avoid camera shake.\n7. Experiment with different lighting, such as natural light or artificial light, to see how it affects the look of the flowers.\n\nBy following these tips, you can create minimalist flower photos that are simple, yet striking.\"",
